.\" robodr-blackbox(1). Source of truth: the USAGE text in
.\" crates/robodr-blackbox/src/bin/robodr-blackbox.rs. Keep the two in sync.
.TH ROBODR\-BLACKBOX 1 "2026-10-30" "RoboDR 0.1.0-alpha.1" "RoboDR Manual"
.SH NAME
robodr\-blackbox \- create black\-box keys, verify and inspect RoboDR black\-box logs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B robodr\-blackbox keygen
.B \-\-out
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-alg
.BR ed25519 | hmac
.BR \-\-allow\-hmac ]
.RB [ \-\-key\-id
.IR ID ]
.RB [ \-\-pub\-out
.IR FILE ]
.PP
.B robodr\-blackbox export\-pub
.I KEYFILE
.RB [ \-\-out
.IR FILE ]
.PP
.B robodr\-blackbox verify
.I DIR
.B \-\-keyring
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-keyring
.IR FILE ]...
.RB [ \-\-checkpoint
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-device
.IR ID ]
.RB [ \-\-allow\-hmac ]
.RB [ \-\-allow\-mixed\-algorithms ]
.RB [ \-\-strict ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.PP
.B robodr\-blackbox rotate
.I DIR
.B \-\-old\-key
.I FILE
.B \-\-new\-key
.I FILE
.B \-\-device
.I ID
.RB [ \-\-previous\-keys
.IR FILE ]...
.RB [ \-\-tpm\-sidecar
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-boot\-id
.IR ID ]
.RB [ \-\-reason
.IR TEXT ]
.RB [ \-\-allow\-hmac ]
.PP
.B robodr\-blackbox inspect
.IR DIR | SEGMENT
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-limit
.IR N ]
.PP
.B robodr\-blackbox anchor\-mark
.I DIR
.B \-\-key
.I FILE
.B \-\-unit
.I ID
.RB [ \-\-out
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-allow\-hmac ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The RoboDR black box is an append\-only, hash\-chained, signed log of evidence
records split into segment files. This tool manages its keys and checks logs.
Secrets are never accepted on the command line (argv is readable by every
process through
.IR /proc ).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B keygen
Write a new key. With
.B \-\-alg ed25519
(the default) two files are written: the secret key file
.I FILE
.RI ( robodr\-blackbox\-key/v2 ,
JSON, the 32\-byte Ed25519 seed, mode 0600) and the public key file
.IR FILE .pub
(or
.BR \-\-pub\-out ;
mode 0644), which can verify but never sign and is safe to distribute.
.B \-\-alg hmac \-\-allow\-hmac
writes a legacy HMAC\-SHA256 key file
.RI ( robodr\-blackbox\-key/v1 ,
0600, no public half) and prints a warning; without
.B \-\-allow\-hmac
it is refused.
Key material is drawn from
.IR /dev/urandom ;
the command fails rather than fall back to weaker randomness. Files are
created exclusively; an existing file or symlink is never overwritten or
written through, and if either target exists nothing is written. Without
.BR \-\-key\-id ,
the key id is derived from the key
.RI ( ed25519: "<16 hex>)."
Prints the key id, never the secret.
.TP
.B export\-pub
Write the public key file of the Ed25519 secret key file
.I KEYFILE
to
.I FILE
(created exclusively, mode 0644; prints the key id) or, without
.BR \-\-out ,
to standard output. An HMAC key has no public half and is refused.
.TP
.B verify
Verify the log in
.I DIR
with every key in the given key or keyring files
.RI ( robodr\-blackbox\-keyring/v1 ),
so a log that spans a key rotation verifies. Public key files
.RI ( FILE .pub)
are accepted whatever their mode. Files holding secret material are refused
if group or others can access them or if they are owned by neither the
current user nor root. Symlinks and non\-regular files are always refused.
An HMAC key is refused unless
.B \-\-allow\-hmac
is given (then a warning is printed); mixing HMAC and Ed25519 keys also needs
.BR \-\-allow\-mixed\-algorithms .
Given a bundle file instead of a directory, an exported
.I RBBXBND1
bundle is verified.
.B \-\-checkpoint
names a trusted checkpoint held off the unit; without it the directory's own
.I checkpoint.json
is used.
.B \-\-device
requires the chain's device id.
.B \-\-strict
also fails on warnings (for example a recovered torn tail).
.B \-\-json
prints the full report as JSON.
.TP
.B rotate
Rotate the black\-box key in place, with the writer
.RB ( robodr\-agentd )
stopped. The log in
.I DIR
of unit
.B \-\-device
is opened with the current secret key
.B \-\-old\-key
(keys retired by an earlier rotation are given as public key or keyring files
with
.BR \-\-previous\-keys ),
a
.I KeyRotation
record signed by the old key names the new key
.B \-\-new\-key
(an Ed25519 secret key file with a new key id; an HMAC target is refused),
and a seal is written under the new key. The chain continues; nothing is
archived or rewritten. Afterwards the writer needs the new key and the old
public key as a previous key
.RB ( robodr\-agentd :
.I blackbox.key_file
and
.IR blackbox.previous_keys ),
and verifiers need both public keys. An HMAC old key (the migration off
HMAC) needs
.BR \-\-allow\-hmac .
Re\-running after a successful rotation reports
.I already rotated
and exits 0.
.B \-\-previous\-keys
files get the checks of robodr\-agentd's
.IR blackbox.previous_keys :
public files only, bound to
.B \-\-device
if bound, owned by root or this user and not group/world\-writable.
The export cursor, checkpoint and head mark are re\-signed under the new key
(a retired key vouches only for positions up to its rotation);
.B \-\-tpm\-sidecar
re\-signs the TPM head anchor's sidecar too (a sidecar under a retired key
is refused).
.B \-\-reason
is recorded;
.B \-\-boot\-id
defaults to this boot's id.
.TP
.B inspect
List the frames of a log directory or of one segment file (sequence number,
kind, flags, time, payload preview), at most
.I N
with
.BR \-\-limit .
No signature is checked: it is a viewer, not a verdict.
.TP
.B anchor\-mark
One\-way remote head anchor: read
.IR DIR /head.json,
check that it is signed by the recorder's secret key file
.BR \-\-key ,
and write the signed mark of robot
.B \-\-unit
to
.I FILE
(created exclusively) or standard output, to be carried through the diode
and applied by
.BR "robodr\-anchor\-receiver ingest" (8).
An HMAC key needs
.BR \-\-allow\-hmac .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; for
.BR verify :
intact (warnings allowed unless
.BR \-\-strict ).
.TP
.B 1
Verification failed (tampering, or warnings with
.BR \-\-strict ).
.TP
.B 2
Usage, I/O or key error, including an argument that is not valid UTF\-8.
.SH NOTES
Ed25519 is the default: the robot keeps the secret file, verifiers get only
.IR FILE .pub
and cannot forge evidence. The Ed25519 implementation is in\-crate and not
audited. HMAC\-SHA256 is the legacy symmetric placeholder: whoever holds the
key can verify and also forge evidence. It is refused unless
.B \-\-allow\-hmac
is given; migrate with
.BR "rotate \-\-allow\-hmac" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR robodr\-agentd (8),
.BR robodr\-replay (1),
.BR robodr\-diode\-unpack (1),
.BR robodr\-anchor\-receiver (8),
/usr/share/doc/robodr/OPERATIONS.md
